-- T6 regression: temporal-context leakage seeded through the WHEN LAST /
-- WHEN NEXT day-iterators, plus the sharing-preservation property.
--
-- The iterators run their predicate once per day under a per-day context
-- ([UnderValidTime d, UnderRulesEffectiveAt d] layered on the enclosing
-- context). Those per-day axes currently have NO readers, so fingerprinted
-- caches must remain VALID across iteration days (sharing preserved), while
-- values seeded during iteration steps under an enclosing `EVAL AS OF
-- SYSTEM TIME` override must NOT leak to ambient reads (and vice versa).
--
-- Harness clock: JL4_FIXED_NOW = 2025-01-31T15:45:30Z; ambient
-- TODAY = DATE OF 31, 1, 2025 = serial 739646.
-- serial(2020-06-15) = 737955.

TIMEZONE IS "Etc/UTC"

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Case 1: seeding during WHEN LAST inside AS OF (probe 05)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

`today snapshot` MEANS TODAY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is today` d MEANS d EQUALS `today snapshot`

-- expected: JUST OF (DATE OF 1, 1, 2020) — steps 5,4,3,2 Jan are FALSE, the
-- snapshot is forced on the first step under the override (= 1 Jan 2020)
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) (`WHEN LAST` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 1 2020) `is today`)

-- expected: DATE OF 31, 1, 2025 (pre-fix: leaked DATE OF 1, 1, 2020)
#EVAL `today snapshot`

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Case 2 (route1-A): iterator ALONE — per-day frames override only unread
-- axes, so the shared cache stays valid across days AND at ambient.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

`shared today A` MEANS DATE_SERIAL TODAY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`on or before shared A` d MEANS DATE_SERIAL d <= `shared today A`

-- expected: JUST OF (DATE OF 10, 1, 2025) (predicate TRUE at the start day)
#EVAL `WHEN NEXT` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) `on or before shared A`

-- expected: 739646 (correct at baseline too; guards against over-invalidation)
#EVAL `shared today A`

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Case 3 (route1-B): inside-out THROUGH the iterator — shared binding first
-- forced during a WHEN LAST step inside an AS OF scope.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

`shared today B` MEANS DATE_SERIAL TODAY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`on or before shared B` d MEANS DATE_SERIAL d <= `shared today B`

-- expected: JUST OF (DATE OF 15, 6, 2020)
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2020) (`WHEN LAST` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2020) `on or before shared B`)

-- expected: 739646 (pre-fix: leaked 737955, the override-scope serial)
#EVAL `shared today B`

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Case 4 (route1-C): outside-in through the iterator — CONTROL FLOW, not
-- just a printed value: the stale ambient cache changed which day WHEN NEXT
-- terminated on (pre-fix it ran ~1697 extra days to 31 Jan 2025).
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

`shared today C` MEANS DATE_SERIAL TODAY

-- expected: 739646 (ambient force; caches the ambient serial)
#EVAL `shared today C`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`equals shared C` d MEANS DATE_SERIAL d EQUALS `shared today C`

-- expected: JUST OF (DATE OF 15, 6, 2020) — under the override the shared
-- binding re-forces to serial(2020-06-15), so the iterator stops after 6
-- steps (pre-fix: JUST OF (DATE OF 31, 1, 2025))
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2020) (`WHEN NEXT` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 6 2020) `equals shared C`)
